sam-sales: Heads-up: BlueAnchor wants a 10-day POC. Scope: streaming receipts -> structured JSON + function call to enrich SKUs. They asked for a tiny drop-in SDK snippet and a hosted vs dedicated ballpark for ~22k tokens/day. Any quick blockers?

kelly-client: Quick constraints: must propagate trace_id with every request, and we need an example webhook showing incremental tool payloads. Latency targets: 200ms single-item, 350ms full receipt.

priya-presales: For POC we recommend hosted low-latency (batching off) + compact model. I'll prep a Node example and a short README on assembling streamed function outputs.

mateo-se: Minimal Node snippet (streaming + function -> webhook):
```js
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference'
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY })
const s = client.chat.stream({
  model: 'redwood-lite-1',
  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Parse receipt -> structured JSON' }],
  functions: [{ name: 'enrich_sku', description: 'lookup catalog & margin' }],
  structured_output: { type: 'json_schema', schema_id: 'receipt_v1' }
})
for await (const ev of s) {
  if (ev.type === 'delta') process.stdout.write(ev.delta)
  if (ev.type === 'function_call') {
    // webhook receives chunked tool payloads
    await fetch(process.env.WEBHOOK, { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify({ trace_id: ev.trace_id, payload: ev.payload, final: ev.final }) })
  }
}
```

alexa-sec: Security: BlueAnchor requires SOC2 + IP allowlist + SAML SSO for prod. For POC enable IP allowlist + scoped API keys with TTL. For prod recommend Dedicated or Private with customer KMS and audit streaming. I'll attach the checklist to the invite.

